#
# The slice the shipped daemon unit runs in (ruled 2026-10-12; see
# docs/design/ARCHIVAL_CHALLENGE_MECHANISM.md section 9.8 and the decision
# log). Its name has no parent, so systemd places it under the root cgroup,
# beside system.slice and user.slice, and the kernel weighs it against them
# as a group: nice values inside a group decide nothing across that line.
#
# CPUWeight=400 against user.slice's default of 100 is 4:1 under
# contention, so a headless staker's daemon keeps about 80 % of the CPU
# while the per-user wallet beside it serves archival shards. The wallet is
# not a system service (per-user custody, as WP-D7 rules on Windows); its
# own defence is the serving runtime's nice 19 and the serving gate. The
# weight is reasoned, not measured: the ledger row shekyl_slice_cpu_weight
# is estimated until the T2 measurement in docs/FOLLOWUPS.md decides
# whether 400 stays, moves, or the slice goes.
[Unit]
Description=Shekyl daemon slice: weighed against user.slice as a group, 4:1
Documentation=https://github.com/Shekyl-Foundation/shekyl-core

[Slice]
CPUWeight=400
